   "reproduction": "unreproduced: this needs a real LAN gate worker plus a reload landing between a land check and its retry. The mechanism is shown from the code at head.",
   "evidence": "src/app.ts:227-229 at head replaces the base's `gateExecutor: this.deps.gateExecutor` with `get gateExecutor() { return factory.deps.gateExecutor; }`, and reloadConfig (app.ts ~245) sets `this.deps.gateExecutor = gate`. In src/land/queue.ts the first check reads `this.deps.gateExecutor` at line 808. The retry reads it again later, at line 829 (inside the retry callback) and at line 833 (`this.deps.gateExecutor?.freshCheckoutFor?.(entry.repo)`). After a reload to a local executor, `freshCheckoutFor` is undefined, so retryFailures runs with `setup: []` (src/gates/run.ts:298) on the local executor. The issue requires that 'A call already running keeps its executor', and runGateExecution pins its executor (gate-execution.ts:18) but the land queue does not."
  }
